the entire  space it's 6.2 inches  bezel to bezel and then when you unfold  the device it is  7.6 inches bezel to bezel so if you were  to compare this to an ipad mini  which is 7.9 inches it is a very  similar size and shape the one advantage  here you have  is straight away it's a 120 hertz  amoled display and if you're not  familiar with 120 hertz  it's significantly smoother and a lot  more user friendly to use  your eyes immediately recognize the  difference so once you make the switch  to 120  from 60 you'll definitely be happy that  you did on the back we can see it  features a triple camera setup  but they don't tell us what these specs  are yet we can however determine it's  going to be very similar to the note 20  series  which means a 12 megapixel ultra wide  camera  a 12 megapixel wide camera and a 64  megapixel  telephoto lens it doesn't appear that  there's any  laser focusing sensors on the back of  this device not in the renders at least  so we probably won't get the camera  features from the note 20 ultra  just the original note 20 series the big  thing that destroyed the zed fold one  was the fact it wasn't dust resistant  water resistant  or basically life proof at all people  started peeling off the screens as soon  as they got it and destroyed it  so that really set samsung back we have  no information if  this one is going to be dust proof  waterproof but they have said it is  more life proof now so we're hoping it's  going to be a little bit more robust  the zed fold 2 comes in two color  options mystic black  and mystic bronze the mystic bronze is  the one that they've been displaying and  pushing very hard  and i'm sure it will do very well across  the world however personally  i will be picking the mystic black  unfolded it is only  six millimeters thin that is an  incredibly  thin device the s20 ultra what i'm  filming on  right now is 8.8 millimeters and once  you put a cover  on it it's probably somewhere closer to  10 or 11  which means when you fold the samsung  zed fold to  it's only going to be in the ranges of  12 to 15 millimeters thick  that's actually not too bad especially  if you're one of those people that's  used to carrying  one of those big clunky wallet cases i'm  not a fan but  if you are it's probably still thinner  than that itself  okay so enough about the specs why do i  think this is  the perfect device for architects in the  world right now in 2020 well it's the  best of both worlds it's a phone  and a tablet at the exact same time that  means you have  the luxury and liberty of using either  or device  and never having to forget one or the  other when you're in sight or when  you're meeting with a client you can  easily pull out your phone  unfold it start drawing on it start  writing notes  or doing whatever you need like you  would on your normal tablet it would be  nice to see  the dex feature incorporated into the  zed fold too  which would allow it to turn into more  of a pc style device  but i think that will probably be only  available to when you actually do plug  it into a computer the triple camera  setup on the back also gives you the  luxury and liberty  of photographing everything you need on  site be it the whole room  finer details or just the generic site  photo  i found that ever since i upgraded to  the s20 ultra i no longer carry around  my big heavy dslr in fact i actually  sold it and got rid of it  now i use the s20 ultra to capture all  my site photos and even  all my marketing photos the ultra wide  lens on the rear  captures the entire room which is  perfect for getting those marketing  shots or just getting  everything in the one shot the main  camera is fantastic  capturing those in the live moments or  just perfect details then you have the  telephoto lens which also has that  ability  of really getting up close and personal  with some textures  so all three cameras combined is like  having a full  dslr kit in your back pocket so samsung  galaxy  z