e back  being a luxury feature for anybody out  in the field  the s20 ultra that i use now has a  premium  camera bump on the back the fold 2  apparently is not going to have those  premium specs  so yes you're going to get decent photos  and everything you need  but you're definitely not going to get  those dslr quality  high-res images that you're really  looking for and finally  i do think this device is the way of the  future but at the moment  it is still probably a little bit too  small to be used as a practical device  at 7.6 inches it's definitely too small  an ipad mini isn't something you can  really use practically on a day-to-day  basis  for something that requires a lot of  graphic  kind of design elements to it i think in  my personal opinion 10.5 inches  the ipad itself ipad ipad as they call  it  is probably the perfect size so if this  device were able to  expand to such a large uh screener  display  that would again make this device so  much better  so just to recap i think that this  device is amazing  but i don't think it's the perfect  device for architects to throw away  all their phones and their tablets just  yet when it gets a little bit more  refined  is dust proof and waterproof potentially  has that  s pen inside it and is a little bit  bigger  on the unfolded display then i think  this device is going to be incredible  anyway that's all from me today guys  thank you so much for watching i hope  you enjoyed the video  if you did make sure you smash that  subscribe button 2020 style  hit the like button to help the  algorithm and as always  i'll see you next monday
 

